# BUILD Skills Sync

If the user says they updated a BUILD skill file in `docs/`, run this from the repo root:

```bash
npm run skills:sync
```

The app serves downloads from private Supabase Storage, so existing skill content updates do not need GitHub push or Vercel deploy.

Confirm success when the terminal shows:

```text
Uploaded <skill-file> to skills
```

Rules:

- Never commit `docs/`.
- Never reveal `.env.local` or Supabase service role keys.
- Never commit `.next/` or `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`.
- For brand-new skills, update `lib/skillsCatalog.ts`, ensure the API route serves the file, run `npm run lint`, then sync.
